
<section class="hero about-hero"><div class="container"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">About The Lexicon Schools</div><h1 class="hero-title">Education Should<br/>Expand a Child’s<br/>Possibilities.</h1><p class="hero-lead">Since 2006, we have been on a journey to create a learning environment where every child can discover who they are and what they can become.</p><div style="width:44px;height:2px;background:var(--orange);margin-top:18px"></div></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img alt="Students in a classroom" src="/assets/images/about/about-hero.webp"/></div></section>
<nav aria-label="About page navigation" class="about-tabs"><div class="container"><a class="active" href="#story">Our Story</a><a href="#philosophy">Our Philosophy</a><a href="#leadership">Leadership</a><a href="#schools">Our Schools</a><a href="#educators">Our Educators</a><a href="#governance">Governance &amp; Affiliations</a></div></nav>
<section class="story" id="story"><div class="container"><div class="story-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Our Story</div><h2>It Started<br/>With a Question.</h2><h3>“What should a school really do for a child?”</h3><p>When our first school opened in Wagholi in 2006, the idea was never to limit education to textbooks, examinations and marks. We wanted to create a school that looked at the child as a whole person — recognising that confidence, values, relationships, strengths and self-belief are shaped just as meaningfully during the school years.</p><p>From Wagholi, the journey expanded to Kalyani Nagar and Hadapsar, and eventually into higher education. While Lexicon has grown, the fundamental belief has remained unchanged: education should expand a person’s possibilities.</p><a class="play-link" href="#philosophy"><i>▶</i> Explore Our Journey →</a></div><img alt="Lexicon school campus" src="/assets/images/about/about-story-campus.webp"/></div>
<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:34px">A Milestone Journey</div><div class="timeline"><div class="time-item"><b>2006</b><p>The Lexicon International<br/>School, Wagholi</p></div><div class="time-item"><b>2012</b><p>The Lexicon International<br/>School, Kalyani Nagar</p></div><div class="time-item"><b>2016</b><p>The Lexicon International<br/>School, Hadapsar</p></div><div class="time-item"><b>Today</b><p>Three schools.<br/>One educational philosophy.</p><a class="text-link" href="/">Explore the wider Lexicon Group</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="philosophy" id="philosophy"><div class="container"><div class="philosophy-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Our Philosophy</div><h2>Believe in Yourself.</h2><div style="width:44px;height:2px;background:var(--orange);margin-top:16px"></div></div><p>It’s at the heart of everything we do — in the way we teach, the opportunities we create and the support we provide.</p></div><div class="philosophy-grid"><article class="philosophy-card"><div class="eyebrow">Our Vision</div><h3>Confident. Compassionate.<br/>Capable. Future Ready.</h3><p>Who we want every child to become.</p></article><article class="philosophy-card"><div class="eyebrow">Our Values</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:18px;line-height:1.22;font-weight:700">Respect<br/>Integrity<br/>Curiosity<br/>Empathy<br/>Perseverance<br/>Collaboration</h3><p>How we want every member of the Lexicon community to think, behave and make choices.</p></article><article class="philosophy-card"><div class="eyebrow">Our Approach</div><h3>LEX360</h3><p>Our educational framework for turning this philosophy into the everyday experience of a Lexicon child.</p><a class="text-link" href="/lex360">Discover LEX360</a></article></div></div></section>
